From 884dd2b55e1941006ddf667a36cc54212a37cb58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: briansp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:45:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: fused hc_mix for BF16 hyper-connection weights
 (bit-identical to the BF16 chain)

Flash-Next GSQ-RCO keeps hc_{attn,ffn}_{down,up,inject} in BF16, so build_hc_mix ran the unfused
decode chain: rms*gamma, mul_mat_vec_f down, scale+silu, mul_mat_vec_f_vb up, dsv4_hc_pre, mul_mat_vec_f
inject - six dispatches per call, 96 calls per token. The BF16 variant of GGML_OP_HC_MIX replays it in
three (rms*gamma; down + inject rows in one grid; up rows of the 4 streams of one column per block with
silu(lo/hc) precomputed per block and the gated collapse), with the same per-thread K order and
reductions, so the output is bit-identical. Only the CUDA/HIP backend implements the BF16 variant, so the
model uses it only when the hc weights are in a non-host buffer; CPU-resident hc weights keep the chain.
LLAMA_HC_MIX_BF16=0 keeps the unfused chain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
